32	 # A Stream Deck at the table
33	 
34	-Runlog's plugin is in the Stream Deck Marketplace, under **Runlog**. Install it and six actions appear in the action list: Connect, Run, Do the next thing, Press, Undo, and Metric. It needs the Stream Deck app at 7.1 or later.
35	+Runlog's plugin is in the Stream Deck Marketplace, under **Runlog**. Install it and seven actions appear in the action list: Connect, Run, Do the next thing, Press, Apply setup, Undo, and Metric. It needs the Stream Deck app at 7.1 or later.
36	 
37	 ## Signing in
38	 
39	 Every key's settings carry the same account block: the Runlog address, **Sign in**, **Sign out**, **Reconnect**, and a line saying who is signed in. Leave the address alone unless you run a copy of your own.
40	 
41	 **Sign in** shows a code and a link. Open the link in a browser, type the code, and you are signed in on the deck; the plugin keeps that sign-in in a file of its own, not in the settings the pages read. Signing in is not connecting: press Connect after.
42	 
43	 ## Connect
44	 
45	 **Connect** opens the connection, and pressing it again closes it. Nothing is open until you press it, and a connection holding no run closes itself after thirty minutes — the key then says _Idle · press to connect_. A deck that is following a run stays up however long the stream goes.
46	@@ -16,21 +16,22 @@ Every other key says **Not connected**, with _press Connect_ beneath it, while t
47	 
48	 ## The run the deck is on
49	 
50	 The deck presses through the page that holds the run, so it only ever sees a run that is synced to your account and open on a page somewhere: the app in a browser tab, a [dock](#guide/dock), or a browser source. With nothing synced the keys say **Not synced**; with runs synced but none open, **No run open**.
51	 
52	 **Run** names the run the deck is following. Press it to cycle through the runs open to you and pin the next one; its settings list the same runs by name. A pin holds: a pinned run that ends says **That run has ended** rather than moving the deck to whichever run went next. Where one run is open and nothing is pinned, the deck follows that one; where several are open and none is pinned, the keys say **Pick a run**.
53	 
54	 ## The keys
55	 
56	 - **Do the next thing** presses whatever the run is waiting on — rolling the table, carrying on, closing the unit, entering the next — and carries the step's own words. Where the step waits on a checklist it ticks everything and presses the step's own button; where it waits on a name, it takes the first suggestion. Tick **Stop at decisions** in its settings and it leaves both to the page.
57	-- **Press** does the one thing you pick in its settings: a move the pack offers, the roll that is waiting, or a preset answer. A setup from your library can be a key too; pressing it changes the run's loadout and hands it out to the tool.
58	+- **Press** does the one thing you pick in its settings: a move the pack offers, the roll that is waiting, or a preset answer.
59	+- **Apply setup** changes the run's loadout to a setup from your library and hands it out to the tool, set in its settings. The list is your library for the pack's tool; a tool has to be attached to the run for the hand-out to reach it.
60	 - **Undo** takes back the last result. It is lit when there is something to take back and dim when there is not.
61	 - **Metric** shows one number and nothing else: the score, the unit, a clock, the last result, the leader, or a counter or resource the pack keeps.
62	 
63	 On a Stream Deck +, Do the next thing and Metric sit on a dial as well as a key. Turning a Metric dial steps through the score, the unit, the clock, the last result and the leader, and a running clock redraws every second.
64	 
65	 A press the run has moved past, or one the page has to take, comes back refused: the key says why for three seconds, then goes back to what it was saying.
66	 
67	 ## Keeping the page awake
68	 
69	 Chrome discards tabs it thinks nobody is looking at, and a discarded tab is a run the deck can no longer see. Keep the run in an OBS dock or a browser source, or exempt Runlog from Memory Saver in the browser's settings.
